Subject: [PATCH] 1047 redfin: AppleCLCD says why it did not start

The one silent path out of AppleCLCD::start() is the provider's start, and a
boot with no "SWEET FB:" line at all cannot tell which of the two it was: the
'sweet,display' node never matched, or it matched and its provider failed.
Both look identical in the klog - no line. Log the match and the failure, so a
dead present path names itself instead of needing a guess.

A klog with the display path dead now says one of:
  "SWEET FB: AppleCLCD::start: display node matched (provider present)"
    then "SWEET FB: AppleCLCD::start: provider start failed"  provider did not start
    or "SWEET FB: no boot framebuffer ..."                    PE console empty
and nothing at all still means the config table never matched the node.
Healthy boots are unchanged: "SWEET FB: AppleCLCD WxH stride ..." as before.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
index 2c96689..f761a45 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -769,7 +769,15 @@ AppleCLCD::start(IOService *provider)
 {
 	PE_Video video;
 
+	/*
+	 * Reaching here means the 'sweet,display' node matched. Without this
+	 * line a klog with no "SWEET FB:" at all is ambiguous: the node never
+	 * matched, or it matched and its provider did not start.
+	 */
+	IOLog("SWEET FB: AppleCLCD::start: display node matched (provider %s)\n",
+	    provider != NULL ? "present" : "NULL");
 	if (!IOService::start(provider)) {
+		IOLog("SWEET FB: AppleCLCD::start: provider start failed\n");
 		return false;
 	}
 	PE_current_console(&video);
